1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,927
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,137
Earth...

3
00:00:06,721 --> 00:00:08,640
Fire...

4
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:10,183
Air.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:12,852
Long ago...

6
00:00:12,936 --> 00:00:14,687
The four nations lived together
in harmony.

7
00:00:14,771 --> 00:00:19,317
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

8
00:00:19,901 --> 00:00:23,780
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements could stop them.

9
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:25,448
But when the world needed him most

10
00:00:25,532 --> 00:00:27,617
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,246
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

12
00:00:31,329 --> 00:00:32,872
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,206 --> 00:00:35,250
And although his airbending
skills were great

14
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:39,003
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,087 --> 00:00:43,091
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:00:43,758 --> 00:00:45,510
( ♪... )

18
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:50,473
( MAN READING )

19
00:00:50,765 --> 00:00:52,684
OZAI: I am proud of you, Prince Zuko.

20
00:00:52,892 --> 00:00:55,812
You slayed the Avatar.

21
00:00:57,021 --> 00:00:59,566
ZUKO: You're so beautiful
when you hate the world.

22
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:01,734
I don't hate you.

23
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:03,027
I don't hate you, too.

24
00:01:05,196 --> 00:01:07,657
I have everything I always wanted.

25
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,617
But it's not at all
how I thought it would be.

26
00:01:09,701 --> 00:01:12,287
The Avatar is alive.

27
00:01:12,453 --> 00:01:13,580
I want you to find him...

28
00:01:13,955 --> 00:01:15,832
...And end him.

29
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:21,629
( ♪... )

30
00:01:23,715 --> 00:01:25,758
( GROWLS )

31
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:29,053
TY LEE: I'm so excited to spend
the weekend on Ember Island.

32
00:01:29,304 --> 00:01:32,265
It's gonna be great to hang out
on the beach and do nothing.

33
00:01:32,807 --> 00:01:34,475
Doing nothing is a waste of time.

34
00:01:34,559 --> 00:01:36,477
We're being sent away on
a forced vacation.

35
00:01:36,561 --> 00:01:37,645
I feel like a child.

36
00:01:37,729 --> 00:01:39,272
Lighten up.

37
00:01:39,355 --> 00:01:40,815
So dad wants to meet
with his advisors alone

38
00:01:40,898 --> 00:01:42,358
without anyone else around.

39
00:01:42,442 --> 00:01:44,110
Don't take it personally.

40
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:47,155
Doesn't your family have
a house on Ember Island?

41
00:01:47,572 --> 00:01:49,449
We used to come every
summer when we were kids.

42
00:01:49,616 --> 00:01:51,034
That must've been fun.

43
00:01:51,451 --> 00:01:53,870
That was a long time ago.

44
00:02:05,381 --> 00:02:08,551
BOTH: Welcome to Ember Island, kids.

45
00:02:20,605 --> 00:02:22,565
It smells like old lady in here.

46
00:02:22,649 --> 00:02:23,900
Gee, I wonder why.

47
00:02:25,735 --> 00:02:27,695
TY LEE: Who are these two beautiful women?

48
00:02:27,904 --> 00:02:29,864
Can't you tell?

49
00:02:29,947 --> 00:02:31,699
- It's Li and me.
- It's Lo and me.

50
00:02:31,824 --> 00:02:33,284
( RETCHES )

51
00:02:33,618 --> 00:02:36,829
Ooh, I love this seashell bedspread.

52
00:02:36,913 --> 00:02:38,498
Are you serious?

53
00:02:38,581 --> 00:02:40,333
It looks like the beach
threw up all over it.

54
00:02:40,792 --> 00:02:42,919
LI: We know you're upset

55
00:02:43,002 --> 00:02:45,755
that you were forced
to come here this weekend.

56
00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:48,591
But Ember Island is a magical place.

57
00:02:49,217 --> 00:02:50,968
Keep an open mind.

58
00:02:51,052 --> 00:02:53,054
Give it a chance.

59
00:02:53,388 --> 00:02:56,474
And it can help you understand
yourselves and each other.

60
00:02:58,267 --> 00:03:01,020
The beach has a special way

61
00:03:01,104 --> 00:03:03,314
of smoothing even the most ragged edges.

62
00:03:04,273 --> 00:03:06,401
( YAWNS )

63
00:03:06,984 --> 00:03:09,487
BOTH: Time to hit the beach.

64
00:03:12,824 --> 00:03:14,826
TOPH: Aang, I know swimming is fun and all

65
00:03:14,909 --> 00:03:17,954
but do you really think you should be
exposing yourself like that?

66
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:19,080
Cover up.

67
00:03:19,247 --> 00:03:21,290
What?
I'm wearing trunks.

68
00:03:21,499 --> 00:03:23,584
I know, it's your tattoos
I'm worried about.

69
00:03:23,668 --> 00:03:25,253
What if someone sees you?

70
00:03:25,336 --> 00:03:26,587
There are walls all around us.

71
00:03:26,671 --> 00:03:27,880
It's completely safe.

72
00:03:29,048 --> 00:03:31,008
( CHIRPS )

73
00:03:32,927 --> 00:03:33,970
AANG: Whoo, hey!

74
00:03:34,053 --> 00:03:36,889
( MOMO CHIRPS )

75
00:03:37,098 --> 00:03:40,727
( LAUGHING )

76
00:03:42,019 --> 00:03:45,606
This has got to be the most
boring job in the Fire Nation.

77
00:03:45,815 --> 00:03:47,734
- Nothing ever happens.
-( SNIFFS )

78
00:03:47,817 --> 00:03:49,944
AANG: Whoa!

79
00:03:53,239 --> 00:03:54,866
Let's go again.

80
00:04:00,371 --> 00:04:02,123
The Avatar's alive.

81
00:04:02,206 --> 00:04:04,292
We better send a messenger hawk
to the Fire Lord.

82
00:04:07,086 --> 00:04:08,087
( HAWK CRIES )

83
00:04:11,799 --> 00:04:13,217
A black ribbon message.

84
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,720
This is so exciting.

85
00:04:15,803 --> 00:04:16,804
( LAUGHS )

86
00:04:34,781 --> 00:04:36,199
CHILDREN: Ahh!

87
00:04:37,241 --> 00:04:39,535
Hey, you need some help unpacking?

88
00:04:39,619 --> 00:04:42,121
- Sure, thanks.
-( GRUNTS )

89
00:04:52,715 --> 00:04:56,260
Could you scooch just
a little bit more to the...

90
00:04:56,803 --> 00:04:58,596
Perfect.

91
00:04:58,721 --> 00:05:00,473
( CHILD LAUGHS )

92
00:05:01,599 --> 00:05:02,683
Here...

93
00:05:02,767 --> 00:05:04,227
This is for you.

94
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:06,187
Why would I want that?

95
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:07,814
I saw it and I thought it was pretty.

96
00:05:08,022 --> 00:05:09,398
Don't girls like stuff like this?

97
00:05:09,607 --> 00:05:11,859
( SCOFFS ) Maybe stupid girls.

98
00:05:12,527 --> 00:05:13,528
Forget it!

99
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:24,789
Wow, thanks.

100
00:05:24,872 --> 00:05:26,499
This is so pretty.

101
00:05:26,582 --> 00:05:28,167
Not as pretty as you are.

102
00:05:28,251 --> 00:05:30,127
That shell's not so great.

103
00:05:30,795 --> 00:05:32,755
Ahem, shade... Shade.

104
00:05:35,842 --> 00:05:38,052
I thought since it's so hot... Here.

105
00:05:39,929 --> 00:05:41,180
Thanks.

106
00:05:41,389 --> 00:05:43,307
This is really refreshing.

107
00:05:49,355 --> 00:05:51,232
Hey, beach bums, we're playing next.

108
00:05:51,315 --> 00:05:53,484
Ty lee, get over here now.

109
00:06:01,075 --> 00:06:04,370
( GIGGLING )

110
00:06:08,749 --> 00:06:10,793
See that girl with the silly pigtails?

111
00:06:11,002 --> 00:06:13,254
When she runs towards the ball

112
00:06:13,504 --> 00:06:15,214
there's just the slightest
hesitation of her left foot.

113
00:06:15,298 --> 00:06:17,592
I'm willing to bet a childhood
injury has weakened her.

114
00:06:17,675 --> 00:06:20,094
Keep serving the ball to her
left and we'll destroy her

115
00:06:20,177 --> 00:06:21,846
and the rest of her team.

116
00:06:22,096 --> 00:06:23,931
Dismissed.

117
00:06:53,169 --> 00:06:55,463
( FIRE CRACKLING )

118
00:06:55,671 --> 00:06:58,799
Yes, we defeated you for all time.

119
00:06:59,008 --> 00:07:02,094
You will never rise from the ashes of your
shame and humiliation.

120
00:07:03,262 --> 00:07:05,598
Well, that was fun.

121
00:07:05,681 --> 00:07:07,350
I'm having a party tonight.

122
00:07:07,558 --> 00:07:08,559
You should come by.

123
00:07:08,768 --> 00:07:09,769
Sure...

124
00:07:09,936 --> 00:07:11,062
I love parties.

125
00:07:11,395 --> 00:07:12,688
Your friend can come, too.

126
00:07:12,772 --> 00:07:15,399
Uh, what about me and my brother?

127
00:07:15,608 --> 00:07:17,193
Aren't you going to invite us?

128
00:07:17,526 --> 00:07:20,237
You don't know who we are, do you?

129
00:07:20,321 --> 00:07:22,239
Don't you know who we are?

130
00:07:22,448 --> 00:07:24,241
We're Chan and Ruon-Jian.

131
00:07:24,450 --> 00:07:25,451
Yeah.

132
00:07:27,578 --> 00:07:29,372
But fine, you're invited.

133
00:07:29,455 --> 00:07:31,415
Just so you know, though

134
00:07:31,624 --> 00:07:33,125
some of the most important teenagers in
the Fire Nation

135
00:07:33,334 --> 00:07:34,961
are gonna be at this party so...

136
00:07:35,169 --> 00:07:36,212
Try and act normal.

137
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,713
We'll do our best.

138
00:07:44,178 --> 00:07:46,138
ZUKO: Why didn't you tell
those guys who we were?

139
00:07:46,222 --> 00:07:47,348
AZULA: I guess I was intrigued.

140
00:07:47,682 --> 00:07:49,600
I'm so used to people worshipping us.

141
00:07:49,725 --> 00:07:51,102
They should.

142
00:07:51,185 --> 00:07:53,145
Yes, I know, and I love it.

143
00:07:53,396 --> 00:07:55,356
But for once, I just wanted to see

144
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:57,441
how people would treat us if
they didn't know who we were.

145
00:07:57,525 --> 00:07:59,443
Like waves washing away

146
00:07:59,527 --> 00:08:01,904
the footprints on the sand

147
00:08:02,154 --> 00:08:05,908
Ember island gives everyone a clean slate.

148
00:08:06,075 --> 00:08:08,703
Ember Island reveals the true you.

149
00:08:11,831 --> 00:08:13,708
- To the party.
- To the party.

150
00:08:13,791 --> 00:08:15,751
( HAWK CRIES )

151
00:08:18,671 --> 00:08:19,672
( CRYING CONTINUES )

152
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,719
( SQUAWKING )

153
00:08:27,888 --> 00:08:28,889
( HAWK CRIES )

154
00:08:31,642 --> 00:08:34,520
( BIRDS CRYING )

155
00:08:58,461 --> 00:09:00,254
Um... You're a little early.

156
00:09:00,463 --> 00:09:01,547
No one's here yet.

157
00:09:01,756 --> 00:09:03,257
I heard you telling someone

158
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,717
You'd be partying from dusk till dawn.

159
00:09:04,925 --> 00:09:07,219
It's dusk so we're here.

160
00:09:07,511 --> 00:09:10,139
But that's just an expression.

161
00:09:10,514 --> 00:09:12,475
We are the perfect party guests.

162
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,643
We arrive right on time
because we are very punctual.

163
00:09:19,732 --> 00:09:21,233
CHAN: All right, listen,
my dad's an admiral.

164
00:09:21,317 --> 00:09:22,526
He has no idea I'm having this party

165
00:09:22,735 --> 00:09:24,528
so don't mess anything up.

166
00:09:26,447 --> 00:09:30,159
That's a sharp outfit, Chan... Careful.

167
00:09:30,284 --> 00:09:33,746
You could puncture the hull
of an Empire-class Fire Nation battleship

168
00:09:33,871 --> 00:09:36,040
leaving thousands to drown at sea...

169
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:40,002
Because it's so sharp.

170
00:09:40,086 --> 00:09:43,297
Um... Thanks.

171
00:09:49,804 --> 00:09:52,306
Hey, first ones here, huh?

172
00:09:52,389 --> 00:09:56,018
He thinks he's so great.

173
00:09:56,227 --> 00:09:58,312
Well, what do you think of him?

174
00:09:58,521 --> 00:10:00,147
I don't have any opinion about him.

175
00:10:00,231 --> 00:10:01,816
I hardly know him.

176
00:10:01,899 --> 00:10:03,984
- You like him, don't you?
-( IRRITATED SIGH )

177
00:10:10,699 --> 00:10:12,660
So how do you know Ty Lee?

178
00:10:12,868 --> 00:10:14,912
I met her at the beach today.

179
00:10:14,995 --> 00:10:17,039
She was pretty impressed
by a sand pagoda that I made for her.

180
00:10:17,248 --> 00:10:20,459
Well, I met her first.

181
00:10:20,668 --> 00:10:24,088
Look, it doesn't matter
who I met first 'cause I like you all.

182
00:10:24,296 --> 00:10:26,215
But which one of us do you like?

183
00:10:26,423 --> 00:10:28,175
- Yeah.
- Tell us.

184
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,052
I don't know, I don't know.

185
00:10:31,762 --> 00:10:32,847
( ALL GRUNT )

186
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:33,931
ALL: Ooh.

187
00:10:34,014 --> 00:10:35,307
Ahh...

188
00:10:35,391 --> 00:10:37,268
Oh, I'm glad you're here.

189
00:10:37,351 --> 00:10:39,353
Those boys won't leave me alone.

190
00:10:39,436 --> 00:10:41,397
I guess they all just like me too much.

191
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,441
Come on, Ty Lee,
you can't be this ignorant.

192
00:10:44,650 --> 00:10:46,527
What are you talking about?

193
00:10:46,735 --> 00:10:49,613
Those boys only like you because
you make it so easy for them.

194
00:10:49,822 --> 00:10:51,782
You're not a challenge-you're a tease.

195
00:10:51,991 --> 00:10:54,326
It's not like they
actually care who you are.

196
00:10:54,451 --> 00:10:56,036
( SOBBING )

197
00:10:56,328 --> 00:10:59,206
OK, OK, calm down.

198
00:10:59,415 --> 00:11:01,083
I didn't mean what I said.

199
00:11:01,167 --> 00:11:04,336
Look, maybe I just said it
because I was a little...

200
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:05,421
( WHISPERS ) Jealous.

201
00:11:05,504 --> 00:11:07,381
What?

202
00:11:07,464 --> 00:11:09,425
You were jealous of me?

203
00:11:09,508 --> 00:11:13,345
Um, but, you're the most beautiful,
smartest, perfect girl in the world.

204
00:11:13,429 --> 00:11:14,972
Well, you're right about all those things.

205
00:11:15,181 --> 00:11:16,932
But for some reason when I meet boys

206
00:11:17,141 --> 00:11:19,393
they act as if I'm going to do
something horrible to them.

207
00:11:19,602 --> 00:11:22,563
( LAUGHS ) But you probably
would do something horrible to them.

208
00:11:22,771 --> 00:11:26,317
I'm sure they're just intimidated by you.

209
00:11:26,525 --> 00:11:28,569
OK, look, if you want a boy to like you

210
00:11:28,777 --> 00:11:30,571
just look at him and smile a lot

211
00:11:30,779 --> 00:11:33,490
and laugh at everything he says
even if it's not funny.

212
00:11:33,574 --> 00:11:38,037
Well, that sounds
really shallow and stupid.

213
00:11:38,245 --> 00:11:39,246
Let's try it.

214
00:11:39,413 --> 00:11:40,873
OK.

215
00:11:41,081 --> 00:11:42,875
( AS BOY ) "Hey, there, sweet sugar cakes.

216
00:11:43,083 --> 00:11:45,252
"How ya likin' this party?"

217
00:11:45,461 --> 00:11:47,546
( LAUGHS GIDDILY )

218
00:11:47,755 --> 00:11:49,340
( SILENCE )

219
00:11:49,548 --> 00:11:52,426
MAI: I'm bored.
ZUKO: I know.

220
00:11:52,509 --> 00:11:54,887
- I'm hungry.
- So what?

221
00:11:55,095 --> 00:11:56,847
So find me some food.

222
00:11:57,056 --> 00:11:58,057
Sure.

223
00:12:01,310 --> 00:12:03,729
Chan, I'm ready for a tour of the house.

224
00:12:07,816 --> 00:12:10,527
CHAN: Is this your first time
on Ember Island?

225
00:12:10,736 --> 00:12:13,072
AZULA: No, I used to come here years ago.

226
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:15,658
It's a great place if you like sand.

227
00:12:15,866 --> 00:12:18,369
( LAUGHING )

228
00:12:18,452 --> 00:12:22,373
Yeah, it's like, "Welcome to Sandy Land."

229
00:12:22,581 --> 00:12:24,667
( BOTH LAUGH )

230
00:12:27,294 --> 00:12:30,756
Your arms look so strong.

231
00:12:30,965 --> 00:12:33,300
Yeah, I know.

232
00:12:36,804 --> 00:12:38,389
You're pretty.

233
00:12:38,472 --> 00:12:40,933
( SWEETLY ) Together, you and I will be...

234
00:12:41,141 --> 00:12:43,560
( FIRMLY ) The strongest couple
in the entire world.

235
00:12:43,644 --> 00:12:45,729
We will dominate the earth!

236
00:12:49,525 --> 00:12:51,944
Uh... I gotta go.

237
00:13:03,747 --> 00:13:05,749
Hey, watch it.

238
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:07,668
That food was for my cranky girlfriend.

239
00:13:13,299 --> 00:13:14,300
Whoa...

240
00:13:15,926 --> 00:13:17,177
What are you doing?

241
00:13:17,386 --> 00:13:18,846
Stop talking to my girlfriend.

242
00:13:19,054 --> 00:13:21,307
Relax, it's just a party.

243
00:13:21,765 --> 00:13:22,766
Uh!

244
00:13:23,976 --> 00:13:26,520
Zuko, what is wrong with you?

245
00:13:26,603 --> 00:13:28,397
What's wrong with me?

246
00:13:28,605 --> 00:13:30,024
Your temper's out of control.

247
00:13:30,232 --> 00:13:32,026
You blow up over every little thing.

248
00:13:32,234 --> 00:13:35,070
You're so impatient and
hot-headed and angry.

249
00:13:35,279 --> 00:13:37,865
Well, at least I feel something...
As opposed to you.

250
00:13:38,073 --> 00:13:39,408
You have no passion for anything.

251
00:13:39,616 --> 00:13:42,161
You're just a big blah.

252
00:13:42,369 --> 00:13:44,538
It's over, Zuko.

253
00:13:44,747 --> 00:13:46,248
We're done.

254
00:13:46,457 --> 00:13:48,625
Who broke my Nana's vase?

255
00:13:50,586 --> 00:13:51,754
That's it, you're out of here.

256
00:13:51,962 --> 00:13:53,589
I was just leaving.

257
00:13:53,672 --> 00:13:56,383
Have fun by yourself, loser boy.

258
00:13:56,925 --> 00:13:58,135
Nice.

259
00:14:06,143 --> 00:14:08,312
( WAVES GENTLY ROLL )

260
00:14:19,490 --> 00:14:20,491
( CHILDREN SHRIEKING )

261
00:14:25,454 --> 00:14:27,122
( BIRD SINGS )

262
00:14:31,377 --> 00:14:33,629
( BABY CRIES )

263
00:15:04,868 --> 00:15:06,453
( BABY LAUGHS )

264
00:15:21,093 --> 00:15:22,177
( METALLIC CLANKING )

265
00:15:25,222 --> 00:15:27,224
Guys, you're all gonna think I'm crazy

266
00:15:27,433 --> 00:15:29,143
but it feels like a metal man is coming.

267
00:15:29,893 --> 00:15:32,438
( GROANS )

268
00:15:44,491 --> 00:15:45,576
( GRUNTS )

269
00:15:47,703 --> 00:15:48,704
( GROANS )

270
00:15:49,788 --> 00:15:51,081
( ALL SCREAM )

271
00:16:04,595 --> 00:16:05,596
( APPA ROARS )

272
00:16:15,606 --> 00:16:17,191
AZULA: I thought
I'd find you here.

273
00:16:17,274 --> 00:16:21,195
Those summers we spent
here seem so long ago.

274
00:16:21,278 --> 00:16:23,614
So much has changed.

275
00:16:23,697 --> 00:16:25,032
Come down to the beach with me.

276
00:16:25,491 --> 00:16:28,076
Come on, this place is depressing.

277
00:16:40,005 --> 00:16:41,215
Hey...

278
00:16:41,423 --> 00:16:43,091
Where's your new boyfriend?

279
00:16:46,428 --> 00:16:48,430
Are you cold?

280
00:16:48,847 --> 00:16:51,308
I'm freezing.

281
00:16:51,642 --> 00:16:53,393
I'll make a fire.

282
00:16:53,477 --> 00:16:56,855
ZUKO: There's plenty of
stuff to burn in there.

283
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:57,981
( GROWLS )

284
00:17:00,817 --> 00:17:02,569
This is crazy.

285
00:17:02,653 --> 00:17:04,905
How can we beat a guy who blows
things up with his mind?

286
00:17:04,988 --> 00:17:05,989
We can.

287
00:17:06,156 --> 00:17:07,199
Jump on Appa.

288
00:17:07,282 --> 00:17:08,325
I'll try to distract him.

289
00:17:23,590 --> 00:17:26,051
( PANTING )

290
00:17:28,345 --> 00:17:31,223
( HEAVY FOOTSTEPS THUD )

291
00:17:39,189 --> 00:17:41,942
( HEAVY FOOTSTEPS CONTINUE )

292
00:18:23,191 --> 00:18:24,735
( APPA GROWLS )

293
00:18:24,943 --> 00:18:27,487
( SIGHS ) I'm OK.

294
00:18:27,696 --> 00:18:28,697
Well, that was random.

295
00:18:28,864 --> 00:18:30,449
I don't think so.

296
00:18:30,532 --> 00:18:33,243
I get the feeling he knows who we are.

297
00:18:33,452 --> 00:18:35,912
( FIRE CRACKLING )

298
00:18:38,415 --> 00:18:40,334
TY LEE: What are you doing?

299
00:18:40,417 --> 00:18:42,044
What does it look like I'm doing.

300
00:18:42,252 --> 00:18:44,588
But it's a painting of your family.

301
00:18:44,671 --> 00:18:45,672
You think I care?

302
00:18:45,756 --> 00:18:47,049
I think you do.

303
00:18:47,174 --> 00:18:50,844
You don't know me, so why don't
you just mind your own business?

304
00:18:51,261 --> 00:18:52,888
Ah, I know you.

305
00:18:53,096 --> 00:18:54,473
No, you don't.

306
00:18:54,556 --> 00:18:56,224
You're stuck in your little Ty Lee world

307
00:18:56,308 --> 00:18:57,934
where everything's great all the time.

308
00:18:58,018 --> 00:18:59,978
Zuko, leave her alone.

309
00:19:00,062 --> 00:19:01,813
( MOCKING ) I'm so pretty, look at me.

310
00:19:01,897 --> 00:19:03,815
I can walk on my hands, whoo!

311
00:19:07,444 --> 00:19:08,779
Circus freak.

312
00:19:08,987 --> 00:19:10,739
( LAUGHS )

313
00:19:10,947 --> 00:19:12,783
Yes, I'm a circus freak.

314
00:19:12,991 --> 00:19:14,826
Go ahead and laugh all you want.

315
00:19:14,993 --> 00:19:17,037
You wanna know why I joined the circus?

316
00:19:17,245 --> 00:19:18,830
Here we go.

317
00:19:18,914 --> 00:19:21,416
TY LEE: Do you have any idea
what my home life was like

318
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:22,834
growing up with six sisters

319
00:19:22,918 --> 00:19:25,128
who look exactly like me?

320
00:19:25,253 --> 00:19:27,756
It was like,
I didn't even have my own name.

321
00:19:27,964 --> 00:19:29,466
I joined the circus because

322
00:19:29,675 --> 00:19:31,885
I was scared of spending
the rest of my life

323
00:19:32,094 --> 00:19:33,929
as part of a matched set.

324
00:19:34,137 --> 00:19:35,472
At least, I'm different now.

325
00:19:35,681 --> 00:19:38,475
Circus freak is a compliment.

326
00:19:38,684 --> 00:19:41,895
Guess that explains why you
need 10 boyfriends, too.

327
00:19:42,104 --> 00:19:43,647
I'm sorry, what?

328
00:19:43,855 --> 00:19:45,607
Attention issues?

329
00:19:45,816 --> 00:19:47,567
You couldn't get enough
attention when you were a kid

330
00:19:47,651 --> 00:19:50,112
so you're trying to make up for it now.

331
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:53,323
Well, what's your excuse, Mai?

332
00:19:53,532 --> 00:19:55,534
You were an only child for 15 years.

333
00:19:55,617 --> 00:19:57,369
But even with all that attention

334
00:19:57,536 --> 00:20:00,455
your aura is this dingy, pasty, gray...

335
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:02,916
I don't believe in auras.

336
00:20:02,999 --> 00:20:05,293
Yeah, you don't believe in anything.

337
00:20:05,377 --> 00:20:09,214
Oh, well, I'm sorry I can't be as
high-strung and crazy as the rest of you.

338
00:20:09,297 --> 00:20:11,216
ZUKO: I'm sorry, too.

339
00:20:11,299 --> 00:20:13,635
I wish you would be
high-strung and crazy for once

340
00:20:13,719 --> 00:20:16,138
instead of keeping all your
feelings bottled up inside.

341
00:20:16,221 --> 00:20:17,889
She just called your aura dingy.

342
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,141
Are you gonna take that?

343
00:20:19,391 --> 00:20:21,309
What do you want from me?

344
00:20:21,393 --> 00:20:24,479
You want a teary confession
about how hard my childhood was?

345
00:20:24,771 --> 00:20:26,398
Well, it wasn't.

346
00:20:26,565 --> 00:20:29,192
I was a rich only child
who got anything I wanted

347
00:20:29,401 --> 00:20:31,403
as long as I behaved...

348
00:20:31,862 --> 00:20:34,156
...And sat still

349
00:20:34,364 --> 00:20:36,783
and didn't speak unless spoken to.

350
00:20:36,992 --> 00:20:39,661
My mother said I had
to keep out of trouble.

351
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:41,997
We had my dad's political
career to think about.

352
00:20:42,205 --> 00:20:44,124
AZULA: Well, that's it, then.

353
00:20:44,332 --> 00:20:46,793
You had a controlling mother
who had certain expectations

354
00:20:46,877 --> 00:20:48,795
and if you strayed from them
you were shut down.

355
00:20:49,129 --> 00:20:51,339
That's why you're afraid
to care about anything

356
00:20:51,548 --> 00:20:52,549
and why you can't express yourself.

357
00:20:52,758 --> 00:20:54,676
You want me to express myself?

358
00:20:54,885 --> 00:20:55,886
Leave me alone!

359
00:20:58,430 --> 00:21:00,682
I like it when you express yourself.

360
00:21:00,891 --> 00:21:01,975
Don't touch me.

361
00:21:02,184 --> 00:21:04,394
I'm still mad at you.

362
00:21:04,603 --> 00:21:07,689
My life hasn't been that easy,
either, Mai.

363
00:21:07,773 --> 00:21:10,317
Whatever. That doesn't excuse the way
you've been acting.

364
00:21:10,650 --> 00:21:12,235
TY LEE: Calm down, you guys.

365
00:21:12,444 --> 00:21:14,654
This much negative energy
is bad for your skin.

366
00:21:14,738 --> 00:21:16,239
You'll totally break out.

367
00:21:16,323 --> 00:21:17,741
ZUKO: Bad skin?

368
00:21:17,824 --> 00:21:19,659
Normal teenagers worry about bad skin.

369
00:21:19,785 --> 00:21:21,661
I don't have that luxury.

370
00:21:21,745 --> 00:21:24,915
My father decided to teach me
a permanent lesson on my face.

371
00:21:25,582 --> 00:21:27,667
Sorry, Zuko, I...

372
00:21:27,751 --> 00:21:30,629
For so long, I thought
that if my dad accepted me, I'd be happy.

373
00:21:30,712 --> 00:21:31,713
I'm back home, now.

374
00:21:31,797 --> 00:21:33,089
My dad talks to me.

375
00:21:33,173 --> 00:21:35,383
Huh, he even thinks I'm a hero.

376
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:36,802
Everything should be perfect, right?

377
00:21:36,885 --> 00:21:39,179
I should be happy now, but I'm not.

378
00:21:39,262 --> 00:21:41,723
I'm angrier than ever
and I don't know why.

379
00:21:42,182 --> 00:21:44,142
There's a simple question
you need to answer then.

380
00:21:44,601 --> 00:21:46,019
Who are you angry at?

381
00:21:46,102 --> 00:21:48,522
No one, I'm just angry.

382
00:21:48,605 --> 00:21:51,191
Yeah, who are you angry at, Zuko?

383
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:54,194
Everyone... I don't know.

384
00:21:54,277 --> 00:21:55,320
Is it Dad?

385
00:21:55,403 --> 00:21:56,696
No, no.

386
00:21:56,905 --> 00:21:57,948
- Your uncle?
- Me?

387
00:21:58,156 --> 00:21:59,991
No, no... No, no.

388
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,284
Then who?

389
00:22:01,493 --> 00:22:02,536
Who are you angry at?

390
00:22:02,619 --> 00:22:03,703
Answer the question, Zuko.

391
00:22:03,787 --> 00:22:05,121
TY LEE: Talk to us.

392
00:22:05,205 --> 00:22:06,206
MAI: Come on, answer the question.

393
00:22:06,289 --> 00:22:07,457
AZULA: Come on, answer it.

394
00:22:08,208 --> 00:22:10,460
ZUKO: I'm angry at myself.

395
00:22:15,465 --> 00:22:16,633
AZULA: Why?

396
00:22:16,842 --> 00:22:19,219
Because I'm confused.

397
00:22:19,302 --> 00:22:21,012
Because I'm not sure I know the difference

398
00:22:21,096 --> 00:22:22,556
between right and wrong anymore.

399
00:22:22,764 --> 00:22:24,015
You're pathetic.

400
00:22:24,474 --> 00:22:27,227
MAI: I know one thing I care about...

401
00:22:27,435 --> 00:22:28,854
I care about you.

402
00:22:30,897 --> 00:22:32,482
( LONE HAND CLAP )

403
00:22:32,566 --> 00:22:36,152
Well, those were wonderful
performances, everyone.

404
00:22:36,361 --> 00:22:39,239
I guess you wouldn't understand,
would you, Azula

405
00:22:39,447 --> 00:22:41,032
because you're just so perfect.

406
00:22:41,241 --> 00:22:43,326
Well, yes, I guess you're right.

407
00:22:43,410 --> 00:22:45,620
I don't have sob stories like all of you.

408
00:22:45,829 --> 00:22:48,582
I could sit here and complain how our mom
liked Zuko more than me

409
00:22:48,665 --> 00:22:51,418
but I don't really care.

410
00:22:51,626 --> 00:22:52,961
My own mother...

411
00:22:53,169 --> 00:22:54,754
Thought I was a monster.

412
00:22:58,008 --> 00:23:02,012
She was right, of course,
but it still hurt.

413
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:04,472
TY LEE: What Lo and Li said came true.

414
00:23:04,681 --> 00:23:06,433
The beach did help us
learn about ourselves.

415
00:23:06,641 --> 00:23:08,727
I feel all smoothed.

416
00:23:08,810 --> 00:23:10,604
I'll always remember this.

417
00:23:10,687 --> 00:23:13,815
You know what would make
this trip really memorable?

418
00:23:17,736 --> 00:23:20,155
We've got some bad news, Chan.

419
00:23:20,363 --> 00:23:21,489
Party's over.

420
00:23:23,241 --> 00:23:24,743
( SCREAMING )

421
00:23:24,826 --> 00:23:25,827
( GRUNTS )

422
00:23:35,795 --> 00:23:36,796
( CRYING LOUDLY )

423
00:23:46,556 --> 00:23:48,099
( ♪... )

424
00:23:48,183 --> 00:23:50,101
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
